<title>INDIA: India 95/96 raw sugar output 17.80 mln t - industry.</title>
<headline>India 95/96 raw sugar output 17.80 mln t - industry.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's sugar output increased by almost 50 percent to 17.80 million tonnes raw value in the 1995/96 (October/September) season from 12.00 million tonnes in 1989/90, Vivek Saraogi, president of the Indian Sugar Mills Association, said on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>Saraogi was speaking at the start of the three-day Asian International Sugar Conference in New Delhi.</p>
<p>He did not give a comparative production figure for 1994/95.</p>
<p>Saraogi said world sugar production from 1989/90 to 1995/96 rose only marginally by 12 percent to 121.80 million tonnes from 109.00 million tonnes.</p>
<p>-- New Delhi newsroom +91-11 301 2024</p>
</text>
